==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{root|is|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{inh|is|non|bíða}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈpiːða/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːða|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|beið|biðu|beðið}}

# [[wait]]
## {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[wait]] {{+obj|is|:eftir(dat)<for whom>}}
##: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu''' eftir mér!|'''Wait''' for me!}}
##: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu'''!|'''Wait'''!}}
## {{lb|is|formal|less|_|common}} to [[wait for]], [[await]] {{+obj|is|gen<for whom>}}
##: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu''' mín.|'''Wait for''' me.}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[wait]], [[pile up]], be [[on the docket]]
#: {{ux|is|[[verkefni|Verkefnin]] '''bíða''' [[í]] [[hrönn|hrönnum]].|The tasks '''are piling up'''.}}
# {{lb|is|transitive}} to [[await]], [[wait for]]; to be on someone's [[to-do list]] {{+obj|is|gen<for what/whom>}}
#: {{ux|is|[[stjórn|Stjórnarinnar]] '''bíða''' [[margur|mörg]] [[verkefni|verkefnin]].|The government has many tasks to get to.}}
#: {{ux|is|[[margur|Mörg]] [[verkefni]] '''bíða''' [[úrlausn|úrlausnar]].|Many projects '''await''' a resolution.}}
# {{+obj|is|acc/gen +:fyrir<qq:optional>(dat)<against whom>}}
## [[receive]]
##: {{syn|is|hljóta|fá|öðlast}}
##: {{coi|is|'''bíða''' [[einhver|e-s]] [[aldrei]] [[bót|bætur]]|never be the same after smth}}
## to [[abide]], [[undergo]], [[suffer]] (some fate, usually something bad)
##: {{coi|is|'''bíða''' [[tjón]]|'''receive''' an injury}}
##: {{ux|is|Karþagómenn '''biðu''' ósigur fyrir Rómverjum.|The Carthaginians '''suffered''' defeat at the hands of the Romans.}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s1|b|ð|e=e|mp=-}}

